# xv6-plus build artifacts (regenerated by `make` / scripts/run-tests.sh).
#
# NOTE: this is deliberately NOT a verbatim copy of upstream xv6-riscv's
# .gitignore. Upstream uses a bare `mkfs` pattern, which is safe there
# only because mkfs/mkfs.c was already tracked before that rule was
# added. In this monorepo, where the whole project is added fresh, a
# bare `mkfs` pattern would match the mkfs/ *directory* itself (gitignore
# patterns with no slash match at any depth) and silently exclude
# mkfs/mkfs.c from being committed at all. So that one path is written
# out explicitly instead. `_*` (built user binaries like user/_cat,
# user/_xtrace) is kept as-is: no tracked file or directory in this
# project starts with `_`, so it has no equivalent collision. See
# docs/upstream-delta.md.

*.o
*.d
*.asm
*.sym
*.img
_*
kernel/kernel
mkfs/mkfs
user/usys.S
.gdbinit
TAGS
*~

# Python test-harness caches (scripts/, tests/)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
